  "published": "2026-11-04T11:41:26.93Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v1.2.0: SALT_TLS_VERIFY=false accepts a self-signed or non-matching certificate (for example an endpoint reached by IP address) for the Salt endpoint only; private networks only. SALT_SSL, the classic collector's older name, also works. TLS send failures log their certificate reason; redirects are no longer followed. v1.1.2: the app's response goes straight to the client while it is copied for Salt, so apps that close the response stream work and are captured; the app runs exactly once per request; streaming responses are no longer buffered. v1.1.1: keeps values other agents (for example a customer's own hosting startup) set in ASPNETCORE_HOSTINGSTARTUPASSEMBLIES, DOTNET_ADDITIONAL_DEPS and DOTNET_SHARED_STORE; Marketplace installs add any missing one of these App Settings (see the README). v1.1.0: .NET Core 3.1 support; virtual-app path prefix in captured URIs. See RELEASE_NOTES.md for complete details.",
  "requireLicenseAcceptance": false,
  "title": "Salt Security Azure App Service Collector",
